  "sentences": [
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Roommates Leah and Sam set a weekly "
        },
        {
          "text": "budget",
          "wordIds": [
            "budget"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " of one hundred and twenty dollars for shared groceries and cleaning supplies."
        }
      ],
      "translation": "室友 Leah 和 Sam 把每週共用的食品雜貨與清潔用品預算訂為一百二十元。"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“"
        },
        {
          "text": "I would rather",
          "phraseIds": [
            "i-would-rather"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " buy less meat than "
        },
        {
          "text": "cut back on",
          "phraseIds": [
            "cut-back-on"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " fresh vegetables,” Leah says."
        }
      ],
      "translation": "Leah 說：「我寧可少買肉，也不想減少新鮮蔬菜。」"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Sam agrees, but asks, “"
        },
        {
          "text": "Does that include",
          "phraseIds": [
            "does-that-include"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " a "
        },
        {
          "text": "reserve",
          "wordIds": [
            "reserve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " for unexpected costs?”"
        }
      ],
      "translation": "Sam 同意，不過他問：「這個金額包含應付意外支出的備用金嗎？」"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "They allow eighty dollars for groceries and twenty-five for supplies, leaving fifteen as a "
        },
        {
          "text": "buffer",
          "wordIds": [
            "buffer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "translation": "他們安排八十元購買食品雜貨、二十五元購買清潔用品，留下十五元作為緩衝金。"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“We can split the total "
        },
        {
          "text": "equally",
          "wordIds": [
            "equally"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "text": "provided that",
          "phraseIds": [
            "provided-that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " personal snacks come from our own money,” Sam suggests."
        }
      ],
      "translation": "Sam 提議：「我們可以平均分攤總額，條件是個人的零食要用自己的錢買。」"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Leah agrees to "
        },
        {
          "text": "contribute",
          "wordIds": [
            "contribute"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " sixty dollars, but adds, “Any spending above the weekly "
        },
        {
          "text": "limit",
          "wordIds": [
            "limit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " needs both of us to agree first.”"
        }
      ],
      "translation": "Leah 同意出六十元，不過她補充：「任何超出每週上限的支出，都要先經過我們兩個人同意。」"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Sam agrees to "
        },
        {
          "text": "contribute",
          "wordIds": [
            "contribute"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " the same amount and says, “"
        },
        {
          "text": "The trade-off is",
          "phraseIds": [
            "the-trade-off-is"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " less "
        },
        {
          "text": "variety",
          "wordIds": [
            "variety"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", but we can keep our spending under control.”"
        }
      ],
      "translation": "Sam 同意出同樣的金額，並說：「代價是選擇少一些，不過我們可以控制支出。」"
    },
    {
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "They will review the plan after two weeks and discuss any changes before raising the "
        },
        {
          "text": "limit",
          "wordIds": [
            "limit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "translation": "他們會在兩週後檢視這個計畫，並在提高上限之前先討論任何調整。"
    }
  ],
